  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new R.C. 2923.26): No federally licensed firearms dealer shall transfer a firearm to any person unless the federally licensed firearms dealer complies with the requirements of 18 U.S.C. 922(t).\nSection 1 (new R.C. 2923.26): No unlicensed transferor shall transfer a firearm to an unlicensed transferee, unless both of the following apply with respect to the transfer of the firearm:\nSection 1 (new R.C. 2923.26): No unlicensed transferee shall receive a firearm from an unlicensed transferor, unless both of the following apply with respect to the transfer of the firearm:\nSection 1 (new R.C. 2923.26): No person shall recklessly violate division (B), (C), or (D) of this section.\nSection 1 (new R.C. 2923.26): Whoever violates division (J)(1) of this section is guilty of illegal transfer of a firearm, and shall be punished as provided in divisions (J)(2)(a) to (c) of this section .\nSection 1 (R.C. 5122.311): Records checks requested by a federally licensed firearms dealer or law enforcement agency pursuant to section 2923.26 of the Revised Code shall be conducted, and results of the checks shall be provided, immediately upon receipt of the request.",
  "higher_law_duty": "Dealer must comply with 18 U.S.C. 922(t) (federal instant-check law) for every transfer."
